four people were killed in an ambush  style shooting overnight at a party in  California investigators say ten people  were shot in a neighborhood in Fresno a  little more than three hours north of  Los Angeles six were wounded Jonathan  Vigliotti has the latest on the  investigation Jonathan what do we know  right now  interracial good morning at least 35  people were gathered in the backyard of  a home to watch football at some point  the group was ambushed by gunfire and  this party of family and friends turned  into a scene of chaos and confusion in  all ten people were shot when police say  a suspect or suspects snuck into the  backyard of the home and opened fire  four people were killed six victims were  taken to the hospital but expected to be  okay detectives went door-to-door  overnight searching for witnesses and  possible security camera footage police  say at this time there is no indication  the victims knew the suspect or suspects  all ten victims were Asian males between  25 and 35 years old police say there  were several women and children at this  party none of them were injured federal  agents from San Francisco are now  assisting in the investigation and  police have not said at this point what  type of weapon was used in the attack a  motive is also unclear as a precaution  police have increased patrols in the  area this morning Tony and we'll stay on  it Jonathan thank you very much
 

